<section class="measure prose" data-reveal style="--i:2">
    <p>
        I'm a software developer in Nairobi. I finished a BSc in Software
        Development at KCA University in 2025, and I spent most of that time
        building things nobody asked for — a ledger for my own money, a study tool
        for the version of me that was too tired to read, bookkeeping for a savings
        group I actually know.
    </p>
    <p>
        That's the pattern, if there is one. I build for someone specific and then
        find out whether it holds. It usually doesn't on the first pass, which is
        the interesting part.
    </p>
    <p>
        What I enjoy is sitting with a messy problem long enough that the software
        becomes obvious. What I'm looking for is a team that wants that kind of
        person — somewhere the unglamorous half of the work is taken seriously.
    </p>
</section>

